# INVWINWF.KEY - a key script of INVWIN, as INVWIN.KEY: F1 in a form in
# Windows Help, with BIN/INVWIN.HLP beside the program
# (INVWIN_WINDATAWF), on the topic of the field with the focus, else of
# the form.  As in INVWINWH, Windows Help's Edit > Copy (CTRL-INS)
# takes the topic's text, its title first, ALT-F4 closes Windows Help
# and gives the form back its focus, and SHIFT-INS pastes the title
# into an edit, which each snapshot shows and the next keys clear.  In
# item 1's form, CTRL-E switching it to edit mode on Category: F1 there
# shows Item: Category, pasted into Type; F1 in Type, Item: Type; F1 on
# the tab strip, no field, the form's The item form.  Esc leaves the
# form, unchanged, and Search > Find text opens Search, whose fields
# have no sections of their own: F1 in its text shows the form's
# Search.  Last, Exit ends INVWIN and Windows Help with it.
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/INVWINWF.SNP is its snapshot.
T ADMIN
K TAB
T Retro1986
K ENTER ENTER CTRL-E F1
S WCAT
K CTRL-INS ALT-F4 ALT-Y SHIFT-INS
S CAT
K HOME SHIFT-END DEL F1 CTRL-INS ALT-F4 SHIFT-INS
S TYPE
K HOME SHIFT-END DEL ALT-C SHIFT-TAB F1 CTRL-INS ALT-F4 ALT-Y SHIFT-INS
S FORM
K HOME SHIFT-END DEL ESC
S LEFT
K ALT-S T F1 CTRL-INS ALT-F4 SHIFT-INS
S SEARCH
K ESC ALT-F X
S GONE
